Steps to follow for Building and Compiling of TEmployee
1.	Go to the project src\com\talentPool\services copy all content from EmployeeService.java.bak and paste it on EmployeeService.java
2.	Open \Projects\TalentPool\Branches\v_3_6_0\build for the files "temployee_build_web_service.bat" "temployee_build_web_service1.bat" and check whether all the paths and project versions are mapped to the current version.
3.	Now go to command prompt go to Projects\TalentPool\Branches\v_3_6_0 \build>temployee_build_web_service.bat and run.
4.	It will generate all java files in the com folder in \Projects\TalentPool\Branches \v_3_6_0\build.
5.	Copy all generated classes from com folder to project folder.
6.	Copy all methods and imports from EmployeeService.java.bak file to EmployeeServiceSoapBindingImpl.java file.
7.	Start Tomcat.
8.	To publish service execute "temployee_build_web_service1.bat" (Make sure tomcat is started)
9.	Copy all generated content at "talentPool" in  \Projects\TalentPool\Branches\v_3_6_0\build\com to temployee com folder so you will have 2 folders temployee and talentpool in temployee com folder.
10.	Now check temployee.


1.	Go to the project src\com\talentPool\services copy all content from VendorService.java.bak* and paste it on VendorService.java
2.	Now go to command prompt go to \Projects\TalentPool\Branches\v_3_6_0\build>build_web_service.bat and run.

NOTE: 
1. If you have any changes in data object files then run JavaToXMLMapping.java class to reflect the changes in mapper xml files.
2. If you add new data object files then add new entry in  JavaToXMLMapping.java and run the class.
3. Same process need to be followed on portal side also if there are any changes in data object files.